                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The description & trailer for this one is pretty accurate. It's a short (90 minutes for me) cozy game following the main character through a journey triggered by a letter he receives. The player manipulates the elevation of terrain around them to navigate the world, although I would not say the puzzle aspect of this game is at all difficult. The game is mainly meant to tell a story in an artistic manner, and it does so well. All the while, the main character reminisces their past, until ultimately the story is resolved at the end of the journey. \n\nThis definitely falls under an artistic game, and the gameplay itself, barring the trivial puzzling element, is purely walking and engaging with those artistic visions. That being said, if you do not enjoy a short story with artistic elements, this isn't the game for you. If you do, it is. The atmosphere and world are well-designed and the player can interact with many things in minor ways that don't impact any of the story, but just make the world feel more alive. \n\nGreat world design, good vision, fitting audio design, cozy gameplay, and the ending did emotionally engage me. This game has all the facets of a well-constructed work of passion.",
